TEXT 0 -200 Left 2 ;Lab A part 2d/2e - volume-velocity source, tube-end RADIATION impedance at the outlet
TEXT 0 -168 Left 2 ;IMPEDANCE analogy: node voltage = pressure [Pa], current = volume velocity [m3/s]. Narrow pipes = R_A + M_A in series, chambers = C_A to GROUND
TEXT 0 -136 Left 2 ;Vs1..Vs7 are 0 V sense sources: I(Vs7) is the volume velocity in the outlet pipe
TEXT 0 240 Left 2 !.param RA=25k MA1=2347.5 MA3=7512.1 MA5=9390.1 MA7=3640.6\n.param CA2=1.1249e-10 CA4=7.1995e-10 CA6=3.0373e-10\n.param MArad=115.18 CArad=3.11e-13 RA1rad=1.62964e+07 RA2rad=3.23021e+07
TEXT 0 360 Left 2 !.ac dec 2000 10 1k
TEXT 0 420 Left 2 ;2d: plot V(p_out) (~ w*MArad*I(Vs7): pipe 7 shortened to 38.77 mm because the effective length already holds the end correction)
TEXT 0 452 Left 2 ;2e: SPL at 10 m (dB of this expression = dB re 20 uPa): 2*pi*frequency*1.18*I(Vs7)/(4*pi*10)/20e-6
